{
  "about": "How the savings figures read, in the terminal, the tray and the app. Read by the Rust test of lumen_core::savings::text (crates/lumen-core/tests/frontend_savings_text.rs) and by the TypeScript tests of savings-text.ts and the headline (lumenator/src/app/savings-text.spec.ts, components/savings-headline/savings-headline.spec.ts), so the window cannot show another figure, sign or label than `lumen` and the tray. Each state's summary names only what the text reads (gross and extraRounds default to net and 0); the tests fill the rest in as an empty summary has it. `app` is what each period's headline box says: the share line (wherever dollars are at API prices), the token figure and its unit, the dollar line in three pieces with the bold figure in the middle (null: none on record), what it is at, the tags beside it, whether it recorded nothing, and why its data is partial. A state's tokensSaved is a number (a band of no width) or a band {low, value, high}, Claude's tokens as the calibration gives them: every surface shows the central value, and `bands` is the band the app gives on the period's ⓘ and `lumen report` beside the figure. `tokensBand` holds the band's own formatting. ≈ is followed by a no-break space.",
